[00:07.15] We told our tales as we sat under
[00:20.74] Morning's sleepy sky
[00:26.13] With all the colours of
[00:32.44] The sunrise shining in our eyes
[00:41.52] One, then another
[00:46.93] With a story of yesterday's life
[01:02.23] Or of a lover who had
[01:04.95] Gone in a moment of strife
[01:11.27] No thought of sleep ever dwells
[01:34.72] Upon the wise man's mind
[01:41.04] Some task or audience
[01:48.25] Stealing every moment of his time
[01:55.47] Thus we have learned to live
[02:01.74] While mortal men
[02:03.56] Stand waiting to die
[02:09.88] How can we do what must be done
[02:17.13] In just one short life
[02:27.96] And if you ask
[02:30.63] Then you must know
[02:32.47] If you still doubt
[02:34.26] You should be told
[02:36.05] It was not we
[02:37.94] That made it so
[02:39.73] It was by those
[02:41.52] Who went before
[02:50.52] And there you sit
[02:52.35] Tomorrow's child
[02:55.03] So full of love
[02:55.95] So full of life
[02:57.73] But you must rise
[02:59.56] To meet the day
[03:02.27] Lest you become another tale
[03:03.19] Another tale ...
[03:08.58] 